  "notes": {
    "raw": "\\*Data above 298 K estimated. \nPhase change: 580 K, melting point of $As_{2}S_{2}$ ; $\\Delta H^{\\circ} = 1.450$ kcal/mol. \nHeat capacity (cal/mol·K) and enthalpy (kcal/mol) equations: \n$$\n\\begin{array}{l} 2 9 8. 1 5 - 5 8 0 \\mathrm{K}: \\quad \\mathrm{Cp} ^ {\\circ} = 1 9. 8 2 7 + 8. 9 3 0 \\times 1 0 ^ {- 3} \\mathrm{T} \\\\ \\mathrm{H} ^ {\\circ} - \\mathrm{H} _ {2 9 8} ^ {\\circ} = 1 9. 8 2 7 \\times 1 0 ^ {- 3} \\mathrm{T} + 4. 4 6 5 \\times 1 0 ^ {- 6} \\mathrm{T} ^ {2} - 6. 3 0 8 \\\\ 5 8 0 - 7 0 0 \\mathrm{K}: \\quad \\mathrm{Cp} ^ {\\circ} = 3 5. 0 0 0 \\\\ \\mathrm{H} ^ {\\circ} - \\mathrm{H} _ {2 9 8} ^ {\\circ} = 3 5. 0 0 0 \\times 1 0 ^ {- 3} \\mathrm{T} - 1 2. 1 5 6 \\\\ \\end{array}\n$$\nReaction equations (kcal/mol): \n$$\n\\begin{array}{l} 2 9 8. 1 5 - 5 8 0 \\mathrm{K}: \\quad \\Delta \\mathrm{Hr} ^ {\\circ} = - 6 4. 6 9 5 + 0. 1 0 2 \\times 1 0 ^ {- 3} \\mathrm{T} + 3. 0 0 3 \\times 1 0 ^ {- 6} \\mathrm{T} ^ {2} - 9 3. 1 0 0 \\mathrm{T} ^ {- 1} \\\\ \\Delta G r ^ {\\circ} = - 6 4. 6 9 5 - 0. 1 0 2 \\times 1 0 ^ {- 3} \\mathrm{TlnT} - 3. 0 0 3 \\times 1 0 ^ {- 6} \\mathrm{T} ^ {2} - 4 6. 5 5 0 \\mathrm{T} ^ {- 1} + 4 3. 2 2 4 \\times 1 0 ^ {- 3} \\mathrm{T} \\\\ 5 8 0 - 7 0 0 \\mathrm{K}: \\quad \\Delta \\mathrm{Hr} ^ {\\circ} = - 7 0. 5 4 3 + 1 5. 2 7 5 \\times 1 0 ^ {- 3} \\mathrm{T} - 1. 4 6 2 \\times 1 0 ^ {- 6} \\mathrm{T} ^ {2} - 9 3. 1 0 0 \\mathrm{T} ^ {- 1} \\\\ \\Delta G r ^ {\\circ} = - 7 0. 5 4 3 - 1 5. 2 7 5 \\times 1 0 ^ {- 3} \\mathrm{TlnT} + 1. 4 6 2 \\times 1 0 ^ {- 6} \\mathrm{T} ^ {2} - 4 6. 5 5 0 \\mathrm{T} ^ {- 1} + 1 4 7. 2 6 4 \\times 1 0 ^ {- 3} \\mathrm{T} \\\\ \\end{array}\n$$\nSource: Data from Mills (80) who estimated all above 298 K. ",
    "lines_raw": [
